webOS SystemUI's popup alerts.

Palm's files from the reference TouchPad's /usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui (webOS CE 3.1.0),
copied unchanged on 2026-11-07: app/SystemManagerAlerts/ (systemmanageralerts.html,
SystemManagerAlerts.js, depends.js) here, and stylesheets/dashboard.css,
stylesheets/notifications.css and the images they name (images/, beside this folder, with notification-small-update.png and notification-large-update.png for the update announcement; five the
stylesheets name aren't on the device either). Abandonware, like the rest of luna-systemui.
Lunacy serves them at their webOS paths and opens the location alert from its System Alerts
app (CoreApps/org.webosarchive.lunacy.systemalerts).

Changed from the packaged app, with codepoet's go-ahead (2026-11-26): webOS CE 3.2.0's
de-branding (the CE project's build/full-ce/hp_wording.py, tag 3.2.0-CE-Release), applied here
by the same rules on 2026-11-26: the pairing alert's "it's not a HP device" reads "it's not a
webOS device", and images/notification-large-appcatalog.png is the webOS App Catalog's icon in
place of HP's shopping bag, the same file as the CE project's
system/usr/lib/luna/system/luna-systemui/images/notification-large-appcatalog.png.
